# Code Preferences

Style: succinct, readable, simple, rigorous. No cleverness for its own sake.

## Shell / Terminal

- **Every shell tool call requires user approval.** Run one logical step per call so each approval is meaningful and failures are obvious.
- Never chain independent commands with `&&`, `;`, or `||`. Run them as separate tool calls.
- This applies inside `docker run ... sh -c "..."` too — run separate `docker run` invocations instead of stuffing multiple commands into one `sh -c` string.
- The only valid reason to combine commands is when they **must** share the same shell context (e.g. `cd dir && make`).

## General

- Prefer standard library solutions before reaching for third-party packages.
- Imports: stdlib first, then third-party, then local.
- No dead code. No commented-out code checked in.
- Error messages should be actionable -- say what went wrong and what to do about it.
